# Introducing AI Chat Lab 

Let’s try using an AI tool in a low-stress way. You have likely used AI before, maybe even daily. For your first time in this series, you will use Code.org’s AI Chat program, **AI Chat Lab**.

<img src="https://images.code.org/d82ce6ee4dc44c9d9ccdf68b2751fc1c-9fa6476e1e62030a0f0814bbc6f006b5-image-1700521543414 (2).png" alt="Code.org AI bot character" style="border-radius:40px; float: right; padding: 10px; height: 200px; clear: both; margin: 0 10px 10px 0;">

Code.org created **AI Chat Lab**, a safe, student-friendly chatbot built into the Code.org platform. It allows students and teachers to explore generative AI in a secure way without leaving the platform.

AI Chat Lab is designed for education, with guardrails to keep the experience safe and appropriate.

* The chatbot supports learning in a guided, structured environment that encourages critical thinking while solving problems.
* Content is monitored to keep it appropriate and productive, making AI Chat Lab a safe space for exploration.

<br>
<p style="font-size: 18px; font-weight: bold; background-color: #F5F7F8; padding: 10px; border-left: 5px solid #8148B2; display: inline-block;"> ➡️ Want to know more about how AI Chat Lab works? Check out the <a href="https://support.code.org/hc/en-us/articles/30162711193741-AI-Chat-Lab-FAQ" target="blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"> FAQ Support Article</a>.
</p>
<br>

During the AI 101 for Educators series, you will use a variety of AI tools, including AI Chat Lab and external LLMs like Gemini, Claude, or ChatGPT.

In the next level you'll interact with AI Chat Lab to learn more about AI.
